8 and had all the expectations  that started fast and then we you know  we stumbled awesome adversity and our  leadership really uh  you know we didn't have enough of it you  know and those big moments and then just  once it started snowballing it went  downhill and then uh you know we saw  losing talent left and right and  i mean  this is how it goes  hey we know we got to let you go but  before you go you got to give everyone  your old spice pitch you don't have to  convince us we're old spice users tell  everyone else why they should be too  well you know what it really comes down  to it is old spice has really made a  commitment to trying to be more involved  in the community and they made a 10-year  commitment to try to raise the  graduation rate across the united states  of america  and in doing so uh we're promoting the  black voice film the documentary uh i  watch this incredible film and it's  really to encourage  uh all of us uh you know especially  black men to just uh to have  self-confidence and reassurance and and  belief and hope that you know you can go  out and do great things you know and  better than just sports but just uh you  know in life and uh and it starts with  you know just uh somebody believing in  them so all spices took the initiative  to really try to  show young black african-american men  that uh they believe in them and uh  they're going to invest in the future  excellent stuff calais congratulations  on walter payton man of the year all the  best this year as you chase the super  bowl and we'll be waiting for that first  ballot hall of fame  uh induction  hopefully appreciate it you're gonna get  there are you talking to elias good luck  man all right  for sure there he is  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

